  ltr | LTR | The contents of the element are explicitly directionally isolated left-to-right text.
  rtl | RTL | The contents of the element are explicitly directionally isolated right-to-left text.
  auto | Auto | The contents of the element are explicitly directionally isolated text, but the direction is to be determined programmatically using the contents of the element (as described below).
text The heuristic used by the state is very crude (it just looks at the first character with a strong directionality, in a manner analogous to the Paragraph Level determination in the bidirectional algorithm). Authors are urged to only use this value as a last resort when the direction of the text is truly unknown and no better server-side heuristic can be applied. success @17,113569,694,81
